From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 14:03:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 03/24] build: make backend builds configurable and cacheable

Teach the workspace Cargo configuration to supply the GNU/Linux cstdint include required by bundled RocksDB 8.10 under GCC 15. Add a Cargo wrapper that resolves only the repository-pinned protoc through mise, supplies installed Clang resource headers to bindgen when needed, and preserves explicit caller overrides.

Parameterize the backend Docker build by Cargo profile, map profiles to their actual artifact output, and preserve explicitly requested debug information instead of stripping it in the runtime stage. Keep the default release-image behavior unchanged and fail when either required executable is absent.

Provision protoc consistently in dependency and final build layers. Keep cargo-chef and the final build on the same architecture-specific target cache, copy final artifacts out of that cache explicitly, and serialize access where cargo-chef cleanup can race another builder.

Enable the pinned nightly Cargo shallow-dependency mode so locked Git dependencies do not fetch complete repository histories. Persist Cargo Git databases, checkouts, and registry data across prepare, cook, and final build steps, and clear stale Git lockfiles only while holding those caches exclusively.

Remove the eager full-workspace just install-js layer. Keep the pinned pnpm and Turbo tools available before dependency cooking, copy package source with the remaining first-party source, and let isolate's real build perform the frozen, scripts-disabled install and the JavaScript builds embedded in the backend. Retain the pnpm store cache on that final layer.

Document local prerequisites, artifact configuration, dependency layering, rollback, and measured build evidence in patches/backend_build_improvements/README.md.

On one constrained builder, the previous Cargo path was stopped after more than 1 hour 20 minutes while repeatedly fetching complete Git histories. With shallow fetches and shared caches, cargo-chef prepare completed in 12 minutes 14 seconds, dependency cooking in 46 seconds, and the final two binaries in about 4 minutes 36 seconds. The then-eager JavaScript install took 13 minutes 20 seconds and included an unrelated Puppeteer download. The image has not been rebuilt after removing that eager install, so no replacement timing is claimed.
